From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Treggat <taggert2222@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:56:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 24/27] sycl : deterministic oneDNN matmuls
 (GGML_SYCL_DNN_DETERMINISTIC)

For f16 GEMMs with a small M x N and a large K, oneDNN's jit:gemm picks
a split-K kernel that adds its partial sums with float atomics, so the
result changes from run to run (up to 2.3e-5 per value; seen on the
48-row ssm_alpha/beta and 1024-row attn_k/v matmuls at batches of about
80..1500 tokens). GGML_SYCL_DNN_DETERMINISTIC=1 (default off) sets
primitive_attr::set_deterministic(true) on the oneDNN matmul
primitives. Shapes that did not use the atomic kernels are unchanged.
Diagnostics: GGML_SYCL_DNN_LOG, GGML_SYCL_NODE_HASH(_FILE); in
test-backend-ops TBO_REPEAT (repeat and compare bit for bit), TBO_SEED.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
